<title>USA: Ohio jobless rate stays at five pct in January.</title>
<headline>Ohio jobless rate stays at five pct in January.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ohio's seasonally adjusted unemployment rate was five percent in January, unchanged from December, the state's bureau of employment services reported late Monday.</p>
<p>The number of jobless workers was 289,000 in January, up from 283,000 in December, the bureau said. The Janaury 1996 unemployment rate was 5.1 percent.</p>
<p>((--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647))</p>
